#
# prima-materia — New Thought: Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How
# to Play It (1925)
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:NewThought, kept apart from
# traditions/new-thought.ttl, which declares the tradition and its works
# (pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife is declared there, not here). The whole book was
# read, pp. 7-95, in the order of its ten chapters; the nodes follow the
# chapters and, within each, the page that carries them. Every source names
# the chapter title as the contents page gives it.
#
# Every record of this harvest was compared with the nodes of
# traditions/new-thought.ttl (the Quimby Manuscripts). No node there carries a
# claim of this book in the same form, so nothing is linked in place of a
# node; where this book states a claim of that file differently, the node
# carries a note beginning "Differs from".
#
# Harvested with two independent extraction passes over the proofread
# transcription, reconciled by offset and word overlap, then integrated by a
# reader of the whole text. Identifiers are pmc:NewThoughtShinn or
# pmp:NewThoughtShinn plus the author's own term in PascalCase. Signs of
# success, conditions of failure and capacities carry a note beginning
# "Counted as". Cases the author tells of clients and others are entered as
# third-party ascriptions, her own as first-person reports.
#


#
# The Game
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGameOfGivingAndReceiving a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life as a game of giving and receiving"@en, "Das Leben als Spiel von Geben und Empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that life is not a fight but a game governed by spiritual law, whose rules she says the two Testaments state; whatever a person sends out in deed or speech comes back to him in kind (hate for hate, love for love, deceit for deceit)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"game of Giving and Receiving\"; \"spiritual law\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Grounded in Gal. 6:7 as interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 7; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFaculty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Imaging faculty externalizes"@en, "Die Vorstellungskraft veräußerlicht sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "She claims that what a person pictures will sooner or later appear in his outer circumstances, so the imagination must be trained to picture only good; the imagination is likened to scissors that keep cutting out the pictures held in mind."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"imaging faculty\"; \"The Scissors of The Mind\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Read from Prov. 4:23; the 'Scissors' phrase is cited as said by others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 7; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDistortedImagination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feared disease pictured until it manifested"@en, "Gefürchtete Krankheit durch Ausmalen herbeigeführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case offered as a warning: a man who kept picturing and reading about a rare illness he dreaded is said to have contracted it and died; distorted imagination is given as the cause."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFaculty fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbyAbsurditasCurat (Quimby Manuscripts, pp. 34-35): there a believed diagnosis makes the patient ill and an absurd remedy undoes it through doubt; here a feared disease, pictured and read about, comes and kills, and no undoing is reported."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, pp. 7-8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnTrainingTheImagingFaculty a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Training the imagination to picture only good"@en, "Schulung der Vorstellungskraft auf das Gute"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deliberately disciplining the picture-making faculty so that it holds only images of good, after first understanding how the mind works ('know thyself')."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bringing in every righteous desire"@en, "Erfüllung jedes rechtmäßigen Herzenswunsches"@de ;
    skos:definition "Someone whose imagination is schooled to picture good alone is said to attract health, riches, love, friendship, full self-expression and his loftiest ideals."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"righteous desire\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTrainingTheImagingFacultyYieldsRighteousDesire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Trained imagination yields one's righteous desires"@en, "Geschulte Vorstellung bringt die rechtmäßigen Wünsche"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training the imagination on good is claimed to produce the fulfilment of righteous desires."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnTrainingTheImagingFaculty ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnThreeDepartmentsOfTheMind a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three departments of mind"@en, "Drei Abteilungen des Geistes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's scheme divides mind into subconscious (directionless power), conscious (the mortal mind that sees appearances) and superconscious (the God Mind, realm of perfect ideas)."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Florence Scovel Shinn, in The Game of Life and How to Play It" ;
    dcterms:date "1925"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"subconscious, conscious and superconscious\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSubconsciousMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Subconscious as directionless power"@en, "Das Unterbewusste als richtungslose Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The subconscious is compared to steam or electricity: power without direction and without inductive reasoning, which executes in fine detail whatever is deeply felt or clearly imaged."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMadeBelieveWidow a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Childhood make-believe as a widow worked out"@en, "Kindliches Witwenspiel verwirklichte sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a woman who as a child played at being a widow later married, lost her husband soon after and wore mourning for years; the author reads it as a subconscious picture working itself out regardless of harm."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSubconsciousMind fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 8; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMortalMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious mind as mortal or carnal mind"@en, "Bewusster Verstand als sterblicher Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conscious mind is the human mind that takes life at face value, seeing death, disaster, illness, poverty and limitation, and it imprints these on the subconscious."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"mortal or carnal mind\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 9; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuperconsciousMind a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Superconscious mind"@en, "Das Überbewusste"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to be the God Mind present in every person and the realm of perfect ideas, containing each person's perfect pattern; elsewhere identified with Divine Mind and Infinite Intelligence within."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "superconscious mind; God Mind" ;
    pm:nameRole "indwelling divine mind, source of perfect ideas and of one's true destiny" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 9; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineDesign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divine Design"@en, "Göttlicher Plan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person is said to have a divine plan, likened to Plato's perfect pattern: a place and work only he can fill. It tends to flash into the conscious mind as an ideal that seems too good to be true, and is his real destiny sent from the Infinite Intelligence within."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"Divine Design\"; \"perfect pattern\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Plato named only as source of the 'perfect pattern' notion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 9; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnThingsThatDoNotBelong a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Striving for what does not belong to one"@en, "Streben nach Nichtzugehörigem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many people, ignorant of their true destiny, pursue things and positions that are not theirs; these, if gained, would bring only failure and discontent."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineDesign fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 9; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNoWordForACertainMan a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not treat to obtain a particular person"@en, "Nicht für eine bestimmte Person behandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author declined a client's request to treat for marriage to one specific man she loved, calling it a breach of spiritual law; she treats only for the 'divine selection'."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnDivineSelection ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"violation of spiritual law\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnDivineSelection a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking the word for the divine selection"@en, "Das Wort für die göttliche Wahl sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of treating for a named person or coveted house, one speaks the word for the right one that is one's own by divine right, holding that if the wished-for one is right it cannot be lost and if not its equivalent will come. She calls asking aright, demanding only what is one's own by divine right, the first and most important step in demonstrating."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"divine selection\"; \"speak the word\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Karma and the Law of Forgiveness, p. 41; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The right mate"@en, "Der richtige Partner"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attaining the partner who belongs to one by divine right."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"divine selection\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineSelectionYieldsRightMan a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Divine-selection treatment brings the right man"@en, "Behandlung für die göttliche Wahl bringt den richtigen Mann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: after the treatment the client lost interest in A. B. and soon met a man who loved her at once and spoke as she had wished; the author presents it as working."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnDivineSelection ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfSubstitution a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of substitution"@en, "Gesetz der Ersetzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a right idea replaces a wrong one, no loss or sacrifice is involved; one receives the equivalent of what was given up."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of substitution\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnKingdom a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Kingdom (of God)"@en, "Das Reich (Gottes)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Read by the author as lying within man and being the realm of right ideas, the divine pattern; seeking it first brings all else (Matt. 6:33)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPowerOfTheWord a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Words shape life"@en, "Worte gestalten das Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following Jesus, the author teaches that a person's words decide his fate; one changes conditions by changing one's words (Matt. 12:37; Prov. 18:21)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIdleWords a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Idle words and jokes bring disaster"@en, "Leere Worte und Scherze bringen Unheil"@de ;
    skos:definition "Careless speech is said to bring misfortune; since the subconscious has no sense of humour, people joke themselves into hardship. Cases: a woman who wished to live in a trunk ended up in one; another who joked about the poorhouse became nearly destitute."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnPowerOfTheWord ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 10; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prosperity, plenty instead of lack"@en, "Wohlstand, Fülle statt Mangel"@de ;
    skos:definition "A condition of lack is said to be changeable to abundance, since the law works in both directions."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"prosperity\"; \"supply\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 11; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnBlessAndMultiply a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Blessing and multiplying money in hand"@en, "Vorhandenes Geld segnen und vermehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blessing the little money one has so that it multiplies, after the example of the loaves and fishes; every person is said to have the power to bless, multiply, heal and prosper."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 11; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnFollowingAHunch a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Following a hunch"@en, "Einer Eingebung folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the treatment, asking oneself whether there is an inner prompting to do something or go somewhere, and acting on it even when reason advises otherwise."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"hunch\"; \"intuition\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 11; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intuition"@en, "Intuition"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explained as being taught from within and called man's unerring guide; treated more fully in a later chapter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
