pmc:NewThoughtShinnDoubtAndFear a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt and fear block every desire"@en, "Zweifel und Furcht blockieren jeden Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only doubt and fear are said to stand between a person and his highest ideals; fear (of lack, failure, sickness, loss, insecurity) is called man's only enemy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 13; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWishWithoutWorrying a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wishing without worrying"@en, "Wünschen ohne Sorge"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one can wish free of worry, every desire is said to be fulfilled at once; fear must first be erased from consciousness."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearErased ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
