pmp:NewThoughtShinnFaithForFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Substituting faith for fear"@en, "Furcht durch Glauben ersetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciously replacing every fear with faith in good."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 13; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInvertedFaith a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear as inverted faith"@en, "Furcht als umgekehrter Glaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear is faith turned the wrong way, faith in evil rather than good; hence one must replace fear with faith (Matt. 8:26)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 13; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnObjectOfTheGame a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Object of the game"@en, "Ziel des Spiels"@de ;
    skos:definition "The goal is to see one's good clearly and wipe out every mental picture of evil, which is done by impressing the subconscious with a realization of good."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 13; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhyWorrySignYieldsFearErased a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "A sign erases a man's fear"@en, "Ein Schild löscht die Furcht eines Mannes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a successful man reports having erased all fear at once after reading such a sign, now holding firmly that only good can come to him."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhyWorrySign ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearErased ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
