pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhyWorrySign a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Impressing the subconscious with a striking statement"@en, "Dem Unterbewussten einen prägnanten Satz einprägen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting a short, forceful statement against worry (here, a printed sign saying worry is pointless since the feared thing likely never comes) sink indelibly into the subconscious."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 13; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearErased a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from fear, conviction that only good comes"@en, "Furchtlosigkeit, Gewissheit des Guten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A settled certainty that nothing but good can enter one's life, so that only good manifests."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 14; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSilentListener a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Subconscious as faithful servant and recorder"@en, "Unterbewusstes als treuer Diener und Aufzeichner"@de ;
    skos:definition "The subconscious is a silent listener always present that records every thought and word, like a phonograph disc recording each note and each cough of a singer, and then carries it out in detail."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"silent listener\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 14; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightOrders a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Give the subconscious the right orders"@en, "Dem Unterbewussten die richtigen Befehle geben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the subconscious obeys exactly, one must take care what one commands it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnSilentListener ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
