pmp:NewThoughtShinnSmashingTheOldRecords a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Smashing the old records"@en, "Die alten Schallplatten zerschlagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spoken aloud with force and conviction: a declaration that by one's word every false record in the subconscious is destroyed and returns to nothing, having come from vain imaginings, and that through the Christ within new perfect records are made of health, riches, love and self-expression."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"untrue record\"; \"the square of life\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 14; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectRecords a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Record-smashing statement makes perfect records"@en, "Zerschlagungsaussage schafft vollkommene Aufzeichnungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The declaration is claimed to replace false subconscious records by records of the four goods."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnSmashingTheOldRecords ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSquareOfLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 14; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnChristWithin a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Christ within"@en, "Der innere Christus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Christ in each person is held to be his redeemer from the curse of karmic law and from every inharmonious condition, the agent through which new perfect records are made, and his fourth-dimensional self made in God's image, which has never failed, been ill, been born or died. Christ is both a person and a principle: the universal God working at the level of the particular."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the Christ within" ;
    pm:nameRole "each person's indwelling redeemer and true divine self" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Game, p. 14; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Karma and the Law of Forgiveness, p. 43; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 92; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSquareOfLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The square of life"@en, "Das Quadrat des Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The four-sided completeness of health, riches, love and full self-expression, which the author calls the square of life: reached through new records in the subconscious it finishes the game, and as the perfect plan of each life it is said to bring perfect happiness and to release hidden talent."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the square of life\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
