pmc:NewThoughtShinnPreparesForFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking for success while preparing for failure"@en, "Erfolg erbitten, Misserfolg vorbereiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "One receives what one has prepared for. Case: a man wanting a debt wiped out spent his time rehearsing what to tell the creditor, which neutralized the treatment; he should have pictured himself paying."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnDiggingDitches fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbyCulpaOperantis (Quimby Manuscripts, p. 55): there a failure is the operator's fault and not the subject's; here the author puts it on the client, whose rehearsal of excuses neutralized her words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 17; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnDiggingDitches a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Digging ditches"@en, "Gräben ausheben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making concrete preparation for what one has asked for while no sign of it is visible, acting as though one already had it; after Elisha's order to fill the valley with ditches before rain (II Kings 3)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"dig my ditches\"; \"active faith\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 17; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnRightApartment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation opening the way to the right apartment"@en, "Affirmation für die richtige Wohnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking Infinite Spirit to clear the path to the proper dwelling, knowing supply meets every demand and that one is unconditioned on the spiritual plane."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTempter a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The tempter"@en, "Der Versucher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identified with the contrary thought, i.e. the reasoning mind, that suggests doubt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightHome a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The right home"@en, "Das richtige Zuhause"@de ;
    skos:definition "Obtaining the right dwelling against the odds."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBlanketsAndTheApartment a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ditch-digging and affirmation secure an apartment"@en, "Gräben und Affirmation sichern eine Wohnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: during a housing shortage a woman spoke the word and bought blankets in advance against doubt; she got an apartment despite over two hundred other applicants."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnRightApartment, pmp:NewThoughtShinnDiggingDitches ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightHome ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
