pmc:NewThoughtShinnArmyOfTheAliens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubts surge up from the subconscious"@en, "Zweifel steigen aus dem Unterbewussten auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thoughts of doubt and fear rise from the subconscious and must be put to flight (the 'army of the aliens'); this is why getting into the spiritual swing is hard for most."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"army of the aliens\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDarkestBeforeTheDawn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Darkest before the dawn"@en, "Am dunkelsten vor der Morgendämmerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: a high statement of truth stirs up the old beliefs of the subconscious, so tormenting thoughts usually come before a large demonstration, depression and the sense that everything goes wrong; the author reads these as age-old doubts coming up so that they can be cast out, a sign that the demonstration is near."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"demonstration\"; \"error is exposed\"."@en ;
    skos:note "A sign that a demonstration is near, not of failure."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success announced in advance: the text tells the student to expect it before the outcome."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 51; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnThanksAlreadyReceived a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving thanks that one has already received"@en, "Danken, schon empfangen zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When doubts and fears rise, or all seems dark before a demonstration, one repeats affirmations of truth and rejoices and gives thanks that the thing is already received, as Jehoshaphat clapped his cymbals while still seemingly surrounded by the enemy; she reads the promise that the answer comes before the call to mean that every good gift is already one's own and waits only to be recognized."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 18; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 51; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnReceivingPresupposesSeeingOneselfReceive a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing oneself receive"@en, "Sich empfangen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One can only receive what one sees oneself receiving; like Israel, one has only the land within one's mental vision."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingToTheVision ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "What one does not see oneself receiving is not received." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 19; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHoldingToTheVisionYieldsRighteousDesire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Holding the vision brings great accomplishments"@en, "Festhalten der Vision bringt große Werke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every great work is said to have been brought into manifestation by holding to the vision."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingToTheVision ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
