pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingToTheVision a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding to the vision"@en, "An der Vision festhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping the picture of the journey's end, unmoved by appearances, rejoicing while still 'in captivity' and thanking that the end is accomplished; then demanding manifestation of what is already received."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"hold to the vision\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 19; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFourthDimensionalWorld a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth-dimensional world of finished ideas"@en, "Vierdimensionale Welt der vollendeten Ideen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jesus is said to have seen through matter to the fourth-dimensional world where everything is already finished and flawless in Divine Mind; health, love, supply, home and friends are completed ideas there and must come through a person, not to him."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"fourth dimensional world\"; \"Divine Mind\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 19; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineMind a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Divine Mind"@en, "Göttlicher Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Equated by the author with man's own superconscious mind, where perfect ideas are registered."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Divine Mind" ;
    pm:nameRole "register of perfect ideas; identical with the superconscious" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 20; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Success in business"@en, "Geschäftlicher Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Success, here raising needed capital within a deadline."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 20; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLostTemper a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Losing one's temper loses one's power"@en, "Wer die Beherrschung verliert, verliert seine Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author diagnoses a refused loan as caused by the man losing his temper, thereby losing his power."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
