pmp:NewThoughtShinnIdentifiedInLove a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment of loving identification with all concerned"@en, "Behandlung liebender Einheit mit allen Beteiligten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treatment declaring the client lovingly at one with the spirit of all persons involved, and asking that the divine idea emerge from the situation."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"treat\"; \"divine idea\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 20; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNeverTooLate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God is never too late"@en, "Gott kommt nie zu spät"@de ;
    skos:definition "God is said to need no time and never to come too late. When a due date passes with nothing received, the author tells the client this is no failure, keeps on treating and has her keep acting in faith; the money comes days later, and the loan comes in the last minutes before the bank closes."@en ;
    skos:note "The first pass held the passed deadline as a failure record. It is not counted as a failure condition: the text names an empty outcome and declares it none, which turns the absence of the result into a delay."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 15; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 20; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLastFifteenMinutes a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Treatment brings the loan at the last minute"@en, "Behandlung bringt den Kredit in letzter Minute"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a man who had to raise fifty thousand dollars returned to the bank, arrived fifteen minutes before closing on the last day and got the loan without question."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnIdentifiedInLove ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 21; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingTheVisionForAnother a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking another to hold the vision"@en, "Einen anderen bitten, die Vision zu halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "When wavering, asking a friend or healer, who stands at a distance from the matter, to see the success, health or prosperity steadily on one's behalf (Matt. 18:19)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"healer\"; \"demonstrate\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 21; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTooCloseToOwnAffairs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being too close to one's own affairs"@en, "Zu nah an den eigenen Angelegenheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person becomes doubtful and fearful about his own matters; hence demonstrating on another's behalf is easier than doing so for oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingTheVisionForAnother fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbyAmiciIncreduli (Quimby Manuscripts, p. 115): there the doubt that undoes the cured comes from sceptical friends; here it comes from being too close to one's own matter, and the friend is the remedy, not the danger. The client's remark that it all sounded fine in the room and terrible outside belongs here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 21; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeesHimSuccessful a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "One believer's vision secures another's success"@en, "Die Vision eines Gläubigen sichert den Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Quoting an observer, she says nobody can fail if one person sees him succeeding, and that many great men owed their success to a wife, sister or friend who held to the perfect pattern."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingTheVisionForAnother ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Prosperity, p. 21; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .


#
# The Power of the Word
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawsForHimself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Making laws for oneself by speech"@en, "Durch Rede sich selbst Gesetze geben"@de ;
    skos:definition "By what he says a person keeps setting laws for himself; a father who always missed his streetcar and a daughter who always caught hers illustrate this, and it explains superstitions."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"psychology of superstitions\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 22; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPsychologyOfSuperstitions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Charms work only through expectancy"@en, "Glücksbringer wirken nur durch Erwartung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A lucky object has no power; belief and word create expectancy in the subconscious that draws a lucky situation. The power behind any such object is God alone."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbySericumOperantis (Quimby Manuscripts, pp. 60-61): there the operator's own belief about silk produces an effect in another person; here the belief of the one who keeps the charm works in his own subconscious as expectancy, and the power behind it is God."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 22; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHigherLaw a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Charms fail once one knows the higher law"@en, "Glücksbringer versagen bei höherer Erkenntnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once spiritually advanced, one cannot return to trusting objects and has to give up 'graven images'."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnPsychologyOfSuperstitions ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 22; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLuckyMonkeys a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trusting lucky charms instead of God"@en, "Glücksbringern statt Gott vertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: two students' businesses suddenly collapsed after they stopped affirming and relied on 'lucky monkeys'."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 23; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnLawOfForgiveness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Calling on the law of forgiveness"@en, "Das Gesetz der Vergebung anrufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Calling on the law of forgiveness, by which a person can neutralize or rub out his mistakes: having put away the false reliance or found why the trouble was attracted, one asks Infinite Spirit to apply the law, gives thanks that the person is under grace rather than law and cannot lose what is hers by divine right, and then acts fearlessly."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of forgiveness\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 23; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Karma and the Law of Forgiveness, p. 43; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRubOutMistakes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Neutralizing one's mistakes"@en, "Eigene Fehler neutralisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The power to cancel the effects of one's own errors."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
