pmc:NewThoughtShinnHorseshoe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Horseshoe as occasion of faith"@en, "Hufeisen als Anlass des Glaubens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a despairing friend found a horseshoe, took it as a sign from God, her hope turned to faith and she later made a fine demonstration; she recognized the power behind it, unlike the monkey owners."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnFaithForFear ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 23; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnOnlyOnePower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Denial of two powers"@en, "Verneinung zweier Mächte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asserting that God is the sole power, so the dreaded omen cannot bring disappointment but instead signifies a happy surprise; used to change a subconscious superstition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 24; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappySurprise a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolving a superstitious belief"@en, "Einen Aberglauben auflösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freeing the subconscious from a belief that some event brings misfortune."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
