pmc:NewThoughtShinnWillingToDoIt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Willingness removes the feared thing"@en, "Bereitschaft beseitigt das Gefürchtete"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one is ready to face a feared situation fearlessly, the situation falls away by itself; fear attracts it, fearlessness removes it. Called the little-understood law of nonresistance."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of nonresistance\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 24; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFallsAwayOfItsOwnWeight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolving an obstacle by fearlessness"@en, "Hindernisauflösung durch Furchtlosigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "A situation faced without fear is said to drop away of its own weight."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
