pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhatHeWishesForAnother a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wishing for others is wishing for oneself"@en, "Was man anderen wünscht, wünscht man sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "What is said about or wished for another returns to the speaker; helping another to success is helping oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 25; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Health, renewal of the body"@en, "Gesundheit, Erneuerung des Körpers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The body is said to be renewable by speaking the word and seeing clearly, with disease wiped out of consciousness."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"healing\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 25; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMentalCorrespondence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Disease has a mental correspondence"@en, "Krankheit hat eine geistige Entsprechung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The metaphysician holds that every illness corresponds to something in the mind, so the soul must be healed before the body."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"mental correspondence\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, pp. 25-26; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHealingPresupposesHealingTheSoul a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Heal the soul before the body"@en, "Erst die Seele, dann der Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bodily healing requires first saving the soul (subconscious) from wrong thinking."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnMysticalMarriage ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The prior step is the restoring of the soul with right ideas, entered at pmc:NewThoughtShinnMysticalMarriage."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 26; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSoul a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The soul"@en, "Die Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identified with the subconscious mind, which needs to be 'saved' from erroneous thought and restored with right ideas (Ps. 23)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 26; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMysticalMarriage a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mystical marriage of soul and spirit"@en, "Mystische Hochzeit von Seele und Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the subconscious is filled with the flawless ideas from the superconscious, the two become one and God and man are one; man then has dominion over mind, body and affairs."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"mystical marriage\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 26; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sickness from violating the law of love"@en, "Krankheit aus Verletzung des Liebesgesetzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "She states that all illness and unhappiness stem from breaking the law of love, and that good-will wins every trick in the game."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of love\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Restated at p. 62: hate, resentment and criticism return like boomerangs laden with sickness, and love, almost a lost art, must be regained."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 26; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnInTheSilence a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working in the silence for good-will"@en, "In der Stille für Wohlwollen arbeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking God not to let one hate the offender, then spending hours in deep inner silence until peace with oneself, the other person and the world is reached; repeated on following nights."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"in the silence\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 27; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSkinDisease a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Silence and good-will heal a skin disease"@en, "Stille und Wohlwollen heilen eine Hautkrankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: an actress, dismissed through a jealous colleague, overcame her hatred in the silence and on the third day reports total healing of a skin disease doctors called incurable; the author says the disease came from subconscious resentment and love fulfilled the law."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnInTheSilence ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 27; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCausesOfDisease a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mental causes of specific diseases"@en, "Geistige Ursachen bestimmter Krankheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author attributes rheumatism to constant criticism (deposits in blood settling in joints), false growths to jealousy, hatred, unforgiveness and fear; every disease comes from a mind not at ease, so one should ask who, not what, is the matter."@en ;
    skos:note "Strong medical claims stated as fact by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 27; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnUnforgiveness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unforgiveness as chief cause of disease"@en, "Unversöhnlichkeit als Hauptursache von Krankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unforgiveness is named the most frequent source of illness, said to harden arteries or liver and impair eyesight. Case: a woman blaming a bad oyster had fallen out with nineteen persons and so attracted it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 27; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAsTheWithinSoTheWithout a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer inharmony shows inner inharmony"@en, "Äußere Disharmonie zeigt innere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every outer inharmony is held to show a mental one, so all of a person's enemies live inside him; as he wakes spiritually he learns that stumbling or falling in the street means stumbling or falling in consciousness. Personality is named one of the final enemies a person overcomes, the planet taking its initiation in love."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"within and without\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the within\"; \"the without\" (from a saying she quotes)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 27; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 72; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoodWill a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sending out good-will and blessings"@en, "Wohlwollen und Segen aussenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The enlightened person works on himself by sending good-will and blessings to everyone, including enemies (Matt. 5:44)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 28; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnBlessingTheRival a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Blessing a rival and releasing the outcome"@en, "Den Rivalen segnen und das Ergebnis loslassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "First wiping out fear, knowing God protects one's interests and the divine idea will emerge (the right item sold by the right person to the right person); holding no critical thought toward the rival, blessing him all day, and being willing to lose if it is not the divine idea."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"divine idea\"; \"nonresistant\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 28; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRivalMachine a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Blessing the rival wins the sale"@en, "Den Rivalen segnen gewinnt den Verkauf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a machinery seller attended the meeting without fear, blessing his competitor; the rival's machine failed and he sold his own easily."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnBlessingTheRival ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnAuraOfProtection, pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 28; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAuraOfProtection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Protection from harm"@en, "Schutz vor Schaden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Good-will is said to surround the sender with a protecting aura, so no weapon against him succeeds; whoever is blessed loses the power to harm."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"aura of protection\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 28; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGoodWillYieldsProtection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Good-will removes outer enemies"@en, "Wohlwollen beseitigt äußere Feinde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love and good-will are said to destroy the enemies within, so that none remain outside."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoodWill ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnAuraOfProtection ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
