#
# Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious)
#

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWalkingUpToTheLion a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Walking up to the lion"@en, "Auf den Löwen zugehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Getting rid of fear by approaching what one fears and being willing to do it: the lion vanishes when faced and pursues when fled. The author applies it to a friend afraid of ladders, told to walk under the next one to show she believes in one power only, and to fear of people (meet them cheerfully), of lack (spend fearlessly) and of germs (stay undisturbed among them)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Power of the Word, p. 24; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 53; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .


#
# The Law of Nonresistance
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfNonresistance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of nonresistance"@en, "Gesetz des Nichtwiderstands"@de ;
    skos:definition "A fully nonresistant person cannot be withstood, like water that the Chinese call the strongest element because it yields. Jesus taught not to resist evil because evil has no reality and so there is nothing to resist (Matt. 5:39)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of nonresistance\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 30; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSoulSleep a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evil as a false self-made law"@en, "Das Böse als selbstgemachtes falsches Gesetz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Evil arises from vain imagination, the belief in two powers (as in the legend of Adam and Eve eating from Maya, the illusion tree); it is a false law made through soul sleep, the soul being hypnotized by the race belief in sin, sickness and death."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"psychoma or soul sleep\"; \"race belief\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 30; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnChildrenOutpictureFears a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Children outpicture others' fears"@en, "Kinder bilden die Ängste anderer ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Children absorb the thoughts of those around them and often manifest their parents' fears; if one does not run one's subconscious, someone else will."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 31; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMotherFear a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Mother-fear"@en, "Mutterangst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mothers are said unwittingly to draw illness and accidents onto their children by holding them in fearful thought and watching for symptoms, since fear pictures vividly what it fears and the pictures objectify unless neutralized; a mother who said her girl had not had the measles yet was preparing the way for them. The author sets this against the old idea that a good mother worries."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnChildrenOutpictureFears ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 31; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 64; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImmunityPresupposesGoodWill a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Right thinking, good-will and fearlessness for immunity"@en, "Rechtes Denken, Wohlwollen, Furchtlosigkeit für Schutz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Immunity to negative influence depends on being established in right thinking, sending out good-will and being without fear."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnImmuneToNegativeThoughts ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoodWill ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 31; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImmuneToNegativeThoughts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Immunity to others' negative thoughts"@en, "Unempfänglichkeit für negative Gedanken anderer"@de ;
    skos:definition "One centred in right thinking, fearless and sending only good-will, is said to be untouchable by others' negative thoughts and to receive only good ones."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
