pmc:NewThoughtShinnResistanceIsHell a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resistance as torment"@en, "Widerstand als Qual"@de ;
    skos:definition "Resistance is called hell because it places a person in a state of torment."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfNonresistance fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 31; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnBaptizingEvents a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Baptizing events 'Success'"@en, "Ereignisse auf den Namen Erfolg taufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A recipe received from a metaphysician: giving every event, especially a failure, the single name 'success', invoking Father, Son and Holy Ghost; the acme of nonresistance."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"baptize it success\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 32; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfTransmutation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Law of transmutation"@en, "Gesetz der Umwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Based on nonresistance: through the spoken word every failure is transmuted into success, and an enemy's arrows into blessings."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"law of transmutation\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 32; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPovertyThoughts a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Catching another's poverty thoughts"@en, "Die Armutsgedanken eines anderen annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman who knew the law of opulence was often thrown together in business with a man who kept talking of lack and limitation; she began to take on his thoughts of poverty, came to dislike him and held him to blame for her own failure. The author reads this as resistance to the situation and a belief in two powers, which the woman undid by blessing him."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfNonresistance ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"poverty thoughts\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the reading of p. 32; the second pass held it as a caution, the first only as the remedy, entered as pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoldenLink."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 32; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSupplyPresupposesFeelingOfOpulence a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling of opulence before supply"@en, "Gefühl der Fülle vor der Versorgung"@de ;
    skos:definition "To demonstrate supply one must first feel that one has already received; the feeling of plenty comes before its manifestation."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnActingRich ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
