pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoldenLink a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Blessing the unwelcome person as one's good"@en, "Den lästigen Menschen als eigenes Gutes segnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognizing one is resisting and seeing two powers, then blessing the person, baptizing the situation 'success' and affirming that, since God is the only power, this person is present for one's good and prosperity; also affirming that each person is a golden link in one's chain of good."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"golden link\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), The Law of Nonresistance, p. 32; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPovertyTalker a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Blessing the poverty-talker brings thousands"@en, "Segen für den Mangelredner bringt Tausende"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: soon after, through the man she had disliked, a woman met someone who paid her several thousand dollars for a service, and the man moved away harmoniously."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoldenLink, pmp:NewThoughtShinnBaptizingEvents ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
