pmc:NewThoughtShinnHoarding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hoarding and saving"@en, "Horten und Sparen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gifts and expenses are called investments, while hoarding and saving are said always to lead to loss and to strike back: a woman who kept back the money for a holiday dinner had exactly that sum stolen, and in the film Greed a woman who hoarded a lottery prize ended scrubbing floors and was murdered for it. Owning property is allowed, but money loved above all or clung to when it is needed brings disease, disaster and its own loss."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty fails."@en ;
