#
# Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious)
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntellectualKnowledge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intellectual knowledge alone gives no results"@en, "Bloß intellektuelles Wissen bringt nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merely knowing the Truth intellectually does not bring results; the subconscious must be impressed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRighteousDesire fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 48; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnCastingTheBurden a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Casting the burden"@en, "Die Last abwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Handing an adverse thought or condition, the burden, over to the superconscious, the Christ within, so that it is made light and dissolved, rather than trying to direct the subconscious with the doubting reasoning mind; the author calls it the easiest way to impress the subconscious. The statement that the burden (of lack, of resentment, or simply this one) is cast upon the inner Christ and one goes free is repeated again and again, at times for hours, silently or aloud, quietly but with determination, like winding up a gramophone."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"casting the burden\"; \"made light\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 48; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 49; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 50; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBurdenMadeLight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Burden as weight under gravitation"@en, "Last als Gewicht unter der Schwerkraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "A metaphysician's analogy: weight comes only from gravitation, so a boulder lifted far above the planet weighs nothing; thus Christ's yoke is easy, having overcome the world vibration in the fourth-dimensional realm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 48; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBattleIsGods a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Superconscious fights man's battle"@en, "Das Überbewusste kämpft des Menschen Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "From Bible passages saying the fight belongs to God, she infers that the superconscious fights for man and relieves him of burdens; carrying a burden violates law, a burden being an adverse thought rooted in the subconscious."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 49; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnReasoningMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Directing the subconscious from reason fails"@en, "Steuerung des Unterbewussten durch Verstand scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Little headway can be made directing the subconscious from the reasoning mind, which is limited and full of doubt and fear."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnCastingTheBurden fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
