pmc:NewThoughtShinnGerms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Germs as products of carnal mind"@en, "Keime als Erzeugnisse des fleischlichen Sinns"@de ;
    skos:definition "One catches germs only when vibrating at their rate, to which fear drags one down; germs do not exist in Divine Mind and are products of vain imagination. Fearlessness in a germ-laden place is said to give immunity."@en ;
    skos:note "Medical claim stated as fact by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Casting the Burden (Impressing the Subconscious), p. 55; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWorldOfTheWondrous a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "World of the Wondrous"@en, "Welt des Wunderbaren"@de ;
    skos:definition "When man realizes evil has no power, release is instant, the material world fades and the fourth-dimensional World of the Wondrous appears (Rev. 21)."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"World of the Wondrous\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
