#
# Love
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInitiationInLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Initiation in love"@en, "Einweihung in die Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone on earth is undergoing an initiation in love; citing Ouspensky's Tertium Organum, love is a cosmic phenomenon that opens the fourth-dimensional world."@en ;
    skos:note "Ouspensky cited approvingly; textual attestation, not mediated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 56; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRealLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love as God in manifestation"@en, "Liebe als Gott in Erscheinung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Real love is selfless, fearless, demands no return; it is called God manifested and the mightiest magnetic power of the universe, drawing its own without seeking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 56; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnJealousy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Jealousy, selfishness and fear lose the beloved"@en, "Eifersucht, Selbstsucht, Furcht verlieren das Geliebte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Selfish, tyrannical or fearful affection loses what it loves; jealousy is love's worst enemy because the imagined betrayal objectifies unless neutralized."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 56; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLovePresupposesGiving a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Give love to receive love"@en, "Liebe geben, um Liebe zu empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One cannot receive what one has never given; perfect love given returns as perfect love from the person or his equivalent."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnPerfectUnselfishLove ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "What has not been given is never received." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 57; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnPerfectUnselfishLove a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving perfect, unselfish love"@en, "Vollkommene, selbstlose Liebe schenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perfecting oneself on the person: giving him love that demands nothing, refraining from criticism or condemnation, and blessing him wherever he is; continuing until no longer disturbed by his conduct."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 57; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSalutingTheDivinity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Saluting the divinity in another"@en, "Das Göttliche im anderen grüßen"@de ;
    skos:definition "After an Indian brotherhood that greeted the divine in every being, even wild animals, declaring to oneself that one sees only the other's divine self, perfect as God sees him, in His image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 57; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCompleteCircle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming a complete circle"@en, "Ein vollständiger Kreis werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: when one has become a 'complete circle', untroubled by the situation and sincerely blessing the other, one will gain his love or draw an equivalent; spontaneous blessing marks real love."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"complete circle\"; \"real love\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success announced in advance: the text tells the student to expect it before the outcome."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 58; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheCap a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Real love brings the lover back as husband"@en, "Echte Liebe bringt den Geliebten als Ehemann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a jealous woman practised blessing and saluting the divinity in the man who left her; one day all suffering ceased, he proposed that evening and they married within a week."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnPerfectUnselfishLove, pmp:NewThoughtShinnSalutingTheDivinity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 58; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEveryManYourTeacher a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every person as one's teacher"@en, "Jeder Mensch als Lehrer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing an old saying, one ought to grow impersonal and take from each person the lesson he teaches, so as to learn one's lessons and be free."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 58; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuffering a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Suffering as result of violated law"@en, "Leid als Folge verletzten Gesetzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Suffering is not needed for growth but follows from breaking spiritual law; few wake from soul sleep without it. Happy people often grow selfish, setting karma in motion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 58; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLackOfAppreciation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Loss through lack of appreciation"@en, "Verlust durch mangelnde Wertschätzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: a wife who often said she cared nothing for married life lost her husband to another woman; the author says she had spoken the word for it and the subconscious unmarried her."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 59; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIndifferentOrCritical a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Indifference and criticism in marriage"@en, "Gleichgültigkeit und Kritik in der Ehe"@de ;
    skos:definition "A wife who becomes indifferent or critical ceases to inspire her husband, who grows restless and unhappy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnRightMan fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
