pmp:NewThoughtShinnSuccessAlreadyPlanned a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Demanding the success already planned"@en, "Den bereits geplanten Erfolg fordern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting aside a discouraging numerology reading, affirming the client is a perfect idea held in the divine mind and demanding the success and prosperity Infinite Intelligence has already planned for him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 60; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNumberTwo a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Demand brings a position and later literary success"@en, "Forderung bringt Stelle und später literarischen Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: within weeks the man had a fine position and later became a successful writer."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnSuccessAlreadyPlanned ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 60; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessPresupposesLoveOfWork a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Love of one's work for success"@en, "Liebe zur Arbeit für Erfolg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Business success requires loving one's work; the artist's best painting is done for love, the pot-boiler is something to live down."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuccessInBusiness ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectSelfExpression ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "No one succeeds in business without it." ;
    skos:note "The prior step is entered as pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectSelfExpression, the work done for love that the author describes as nearly play; the text names love of one's work and gives no separate node for it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 60; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnContemptForMoney a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contempt for money separates from it"@en, "Verachtung des Geldes trennt davon"@de ;
    skos:definition "Disdaining money and the people who have it keeps one poor, which is said to explain poor artists; to attract something one must be in accord with it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 60; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMoneyGodInManifestation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Money as God in manifestation"@en, "Geld als Gott in Erscheinung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Money is called God manifested as release from want and limitation; it must circulate and be rightly used, and the universal bank she speaks of never fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 60; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPathOfLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Path of love versus path of greed"@en, "Weg der Liebe gegen Weg der Gier"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since God is both love and supply, the path of love brings everything, while selfishness and greed make supply vanish."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 61; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLawOfUse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The law of use"@en, "Das Gesetz des Gebrauchs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping things unused is named a violation of the law of use for which the body pays: a rich woman who stored away sixty-seven necklaces and clothes she never wore is said to have had her arms grow paralysed from holding on and to have lost control of her wealth, and a student's congestion is traced to furniture kept in storage."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the law of use\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 61; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 69; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnCleaningConsciousnessOfResentment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cleaning consciousness of resentment"@en, "Das Bewusstsein von Groll reinigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working month after month, under the teacher's guidance, to clear one's consciousness of resentment until even the last resented person is met with love."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Love, p. 62; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMarvelousLightness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cleared resentment turns an enemy kind"@en, "Getilgter Groll macht Gegnerin freundlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: once all resentment was wiped out, the student answered a remark with kindness, the other woman apologized and became lovely to her; she reports marvellous inner lightness."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnCleaningConsciousnessOfResentment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnLovingHarmoniousHappy ;
