#
# Intuition or Guidance
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWordAndIntuitiveLeads a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Word plus intuitive lead accomplish anything"@en, "Wort plus Eingebung vollbringen alles"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nothing is too great for one who understands his word's power and follows intuitive leads; the word sets unseen forces in motion that can rebuild the body or remould affairs, so affirmations must be chosen carefully."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 66; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLead a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking the word, then demanding a lead"@en, "Das Wort sprechen, dann einen Hinweis fordern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's answer to how to make a demonstration: speak the word, then do nothing until a definite lead comes; demand it by asking Infinite Spirit to reveal the way and whether there is anything to do. The answer comes as hunch, chance remark, or something read."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"demonstration\"; \"definite lead\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 66; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnActionPresupposesDefiniteLead a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Wait for the lead before acting"@en, "Vor dem Handeln den Hinweis abwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "After speaking the word, action is to follow only once a definite lead has come."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnFollowingAHunch ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLead ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 66; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHowToMakeADemonstration a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "How to make a demonstration"@en, "Wie man eine Demonstration herbeiführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three steps in the order the source gives them as its answer to how a demonstration is made: speaking the word; doing nothing further while demanding and awaiting a definite lead; acting on the lead when it comes as a hunch, a chance remark or a passage read."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:NewThoughtShinnSpeakingTheWord ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLead ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:NewThoughtShinnFollowingAHunch ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The author answers the question how to make a demonstration with a fixed order: the word is spoken first, then nothing is done until a definite lead has been demanded and received, and only then is the lead followed. The waiting has its sense only between the word and the lead, and acting has its sense only as obedience to a lead; the same order returns where she says a demonstration forced through reasoning stops and one should act only on intuition or definite leads." ;
    skos:note "The pair from lead to action is entered as pmc:NewThoughtShinnActionPresupposesDefiniteLead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 66; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 67; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing", "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 91; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnAvalanchesOfAbundance a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation for immediate supply in avalanches"@en, "Affirmation sofortiger Versorgung in Lawinen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking Infinite Spirit to open the way for immediate supply and let everything rightfully one's own arrive in great abundance, then asking for a definite lead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 67; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnAnotherLead a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting for a confirming lead"@en, "Auf einen bestätigenden Hinweis warten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before acting on a lead involving money, waiting for a second, unmistakable lead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 67; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHundredDollarGift a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following the lead to give brings a large sum"@en, "Der Eingebung zu geben folgen bringt große Summe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Case: the lead was to give a hundred dollars to a spiritual helper; a confirming second lead came by a stranger's remark, she gave, and soon a large sum came remarkably."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnAvalanchesOfAbundance, pmp:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLead, pmp:NewThoughtShinnTithing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty ;
