pmp:NewThoughtShinnTithing a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tithing and cheerful giving"@en, "Zehnter und fröhliches Geben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Giving to create activity in finances, above all tithing a tenth of one's income, which the author says has never failed, in her knowledge, as an investment; the gift must be made with love and cheerfulness, bills paid cheerfully and all money sent out fearlessly with a blessing, an attitude said to make one master of money."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"tithing\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 67; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTithingYieldsPlenty a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tithing brings increase"@en, "Der Zehnte bringt Mehrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tithing is said surely to bring increase; the tenth returns blessed and multiplied, many of the richest have tithed, and the author has never seen it fail."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnTithing ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlenty ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
