pmc:NewThoughtShinnPsychicPlane a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against psychic guidance"@en, "Gegen Führung aus der psychischen Ebene"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author rejects seeking guidance from the psychic plane, a level of numerous minds and of opposites produced by mortal thought, not the One Mind; opening to it makes one a target of destructive forces."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"psychic plane\"; \"The One Mind\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a dispute: the author rejects the practice named; the other side is not read and is entered only as she reports it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbyDiagnosisEstOpinio (Quimby Manuscripts, p. 32): there the clairvoyant subject is found to read the belief of those present and is given up for that reason; here the psychic plane is refused as a plane of many minds and of opposites, from which good or bad messages may come."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Intuition or Guidance, p. 71; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTargetForDestructiveForces a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Opening to subjectivity invites destructive forces"@en, "Öffnung für Subjektivität lädt zerstörerische Kräfte ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning that opening the mind to the psychic plane exposes one to good or bad messages and destructive forces."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLead ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
