pmc:NewThoughtShinnSin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Metaphysical meaning of sin"@en, "Metaphysische Bedeutung von Sünde"@de ;
    skos:definition "In metaphysics sin is broader than in old teaching: whatever is not of faith; fear and worry count as deadly sins, inverted faith that brings about what is feared. Maeterlinck's phrase that man is God afraid is cited."@en ;
    skos:note "Maeterlinck quoted with approval."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
