pmp:NewThoughtShinnDenialsAndAffirmations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Denials and affirmations"@en, "Verneinungen und Bejahungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rule that every denial is to be followed by an affirmation: one first denies the appearance (of disease, loss, separation) as unreal, then affirms the perfect idea in its place; the chapter of the same name gives the forms."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 90; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnAbsentTreatment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Absent healing treatment"@en, "Fernheilungsbehandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating an unseen sick person by denying the appearance of disease as unreal and unable to register in his consciousness, then affirming him a flawless idea held by the divine mind, pure substance that expresses perfection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 90; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAbsentTreatmentInstantaneous a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Absent treatment works instantly at any distance"@en, "Fernbehandlung wirkt sofort über jede Entfernung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since Divine Mind knows neither time nor space the word reaches its goal instantly; the author reports instantaneous results treating patients in Europe."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnAbsentTreatment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnBodyRenewed ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:QuimbyAbsensWhitney (Quimby Manuscripts, pp. 105-106): there the healer withdraws for an hour at an appointed time and the result is checked against witnesses in the patient's house; here the author speaks a statement on a telephone call late at night and holds the result instantaneous because Divine Mind knows no time or space, and no check is named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 91; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnVisualizingAndVisioning a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualizing versus visioning"@en, "Visualisieren gegenüber Schauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author distinguishes visualizing, a mental process of the reasoning mind, from visioning, a spiritual process directed by intuition, i.e. the superconscious; the student should train to receive flashes and work them out through definite leads."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Florence Scovel Shinn, in The Game of Life and How to Play It" ;
    dcterms:date "1925"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"visualizing\"; \"visioning\"; \"divine pictures\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 91; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnOnlyThatWhichGodDesires a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Desiring only what God desires"@en, "Nur wünschen, was Gott wünscht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declaring that one wants only what God wants for one, so false desires fade and new blueprints come from the God within."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 91; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNewBlueprints a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Surrender of desire brings God's plan"@en, "Hingabe des Wunsches bringt Gottes Plan"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desiring only God's will is said to dissolve false desires and give one the divine plan (a palace rather than a bungalow)."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnOnlyThatWhichGodDesires ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnSquareOfLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Game of Life and How to Play It (Marina del Rey, CA: DeVorss & Company, n.d.; copyright 1925, ISBN 0-87516-257-6), Denials and Affirmations, p. 91; read in the proofread transcription Project Gutenberg eBook #74878 (2024), made from the archive.org scan gameoflifehowtop00shin of this printing" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMasterArchitect a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Master Architect"@en, "Meisterarchitekt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The God within, who gives new blueprints once false desires fade; his plan exceeds reason and always forms the square of life."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Master Architect; the God within" ;
    pm:nameRole "designer of each person's life plan" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnGameOfLife ;
